			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Cache product identity and simplify replacement logic\n\nReplace the `fileURLToPath`-driven path resolution with `new URL(import.meta.url).pathname` for a lighter dependency footprint. Introduce a `Cached` variable so `product.json` is parsed once per process, and add an explicit `ProductInfo` interface with typed fallback default values for when the file cannot be read.\n\nRemove the broken idempotency guard in the replacement loop — the `if (Current.includes(To) && Current.includes(From))` check never actually skipped replacements — and mark return values with `as const` for tighter type inference. Fix the `TransformPlugin` import path from `\"../../../Type.js\"` to `\"../../Type.js\"`.\n\nThe Tauri channel buffer import in Service.ts is reformatted for readability only, with no behavioral change.",
			"SHA": "ed58cb9f4589ea83119b19e7b7c5e55e07d0d5a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T02:23:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				768,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Output): Add GitHub badge badges and restore funding logo table\n\nAdd a header badge table showing last-commit, issues, stars, and downloads for quick repository status at a glance. Replace the previous inline SVG footer with an HTML table of properly sized logo images (Land, PlayForm, NLnet, NGI0 Commons Fund) linking to their respective sites.\n\nRe-wrap long lines throughout the document to improve readability without diff noise in future changes. Tighten dashes in em dash contexts and align table formatting with plain pipe-delimited syntax for cleaner markdown.\n\nThe README now provides immediate repository metadata on open and restores visually recognizable partner logos in the funding section.",
			"SHA": "f22c8b44525a362f2770c012395f615e2692f5af"
		}
